<.shell current={:ai_writing}>
  <h1>AI writing</h1>
  <p class="lead">Asks in plain words, and AI's replies, beside what it changes.</p>

  <div class="demo">
    <.ai_editor id="ai-writing-demo" ai?={true} column_id="ai-writing-demo-column">
      <:head>
        <p class="title mb-2">Task report</p>
        <p class="hint">The head: the title, the description, and the page's links.</p>
      </:head>
      <:column>
        <.ai_writing
          id="ai-writing-demo-ai"
          ai={:ok}
          form={ask_form("")}
          asks={SampleData.ai_asks()}
          label="Ask AI"
          button="Ask"
          sees="AI sees the agency's form and your team's field names, never its members or records."
          start_over="Start over? Your changes and the conversation go. Task report goes back to version 3, as saved."
        />
      </:column>
      <p class="hint">The page's main part: the report, or the form tried on an activity.</p>
    </.ai_editor>
  </div>

  <h3>An ask running</h3>
  <div class="demo">
    <div class="measure">
      <.ai_writing
        id="ai-writing-demo-running"
        ai={:ok}
        form={ask_form("")}
        asks={[]}
        pending={%{ask: "Write this form."}}
        label="Ask AI"
        button="Ask"
        sees="AI sees your team's field names, never its members or records."
      />
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3>An ask that failed</h3>
  <p>
    It stays in the conversation with what went wrong and what to try, never a toast.
    Ask again runs it in its place when that could work.
  </p>
  <div class="demo">
    <div class="measure">
      <.ai_writing
        id="ai-writing-demo-failed"
        ai={:ok}
        form={ask_form("")}
        asks={[
          %{
            id: 1,
            ask: "Group by quarter",
            note: nil,
            undo?: false,
            next: [],
            failed: failed(:too_many_steps, "query")
          }
        ]}
        label="Ask AI"
        button="Ask"
        sees="AI sees your team's field names, never its members or records."
      />
    </div>
  </div>

  <h3>A draft waiting</h3>
  <p>
    On the report's or the form's page, only to the person whose draft it is. Discard them
    asks first, as Start over does.
  </p>
  <div class="demo">
    <.draft_waiting
      id="ai-writing-demo-draft"
      draft={%{updated_at: DateTime.add(DateTime.utc_now(), -20, :minute), asks: [%{}, %{}]}}
      name="Task report"
      change="Change form"
      change_path="#"
      timezone="America/Vancouver"
    />
  </div>

  <h3>Closed</h3>
  <div class="demo">
    <div class="measure">
      <.ai_writing
        id="ai-writing-demo-closed"
        ai={{:error, :paused}}
        form={ask_form("")}
        asks={[]}
        label="Ask AI"
        button="Ask"
        closed="AI writing is paused until next month. You can still change the query yourself."
        sees="AI sees your team's field names, never its members or records."
      />
    </div>
  </div>

  <h2>When to use</h2>
  <p>
    A page AI writes for an admin: Change report and Change form. From 1024px the column
    starts beside the title and stays in view as the page scrolls, down to the Save bar at
    the window's foot, and its conversation scrolls on its own. Under that it's one column:
    the head, AI writing, then the page, with the last two asks and Show earlier asks.
  </p>

  <h2>How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      The asks show as a conversation, oldest first: each ask on the right, AI's reply under it.
    </li>
    <li>A reply that changed the page has Undo, which puts it back to before that ask.</li>
    <li>A form's reply ends with Left blank: each label AI didn't fill, and why.</li>
    <li>
      A running ask shows at once, with Thinking…, the seconds it has taken, and Stop. The box
      clears and its button waits. No steps: they change too fast to read.
    </li>
    <li>
      Try next, under the newest reply: two or three asks AI suggests. A tap puts one in the
      box, to change or send; it never sends on its own.
    </li>
    <li>The line under the heading says what AI sees, and links to How it works.</li>
    <li>Enter sends; Shift+Enter starts a new line.</li>
    <li>
      Each ask and each change by hand is kept as the person's draft, so the page opens
      again as they left it, with a toast saying when it's from. Start over, under the box,
      asks first, then discards it and goes back to what's saved.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>In the app</h2>
  <p>
    <code>&lt;.ai_editor&gt;</code>
    and <code>&lt;.ai_writing&gt;</code>
    and <code>&lt;.draft_waiting&gt;</code>
    in <code>Web.Components.AIWriting</code>. The page runs each ask with
    <code>App.Operation.AskAI</code>
    and keeps the conversation as a draft with <code>App.Operation.SaveDraft</code>.
  </p>
</.shell>
